{"tool_name":"dna_chisel","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"DNA_Chisel","home":"https://edinburgh-genome-foundry.github.io/","license":"MIT","summary":"DNA Chisel - A versatile sequence optimizer.\nDNA Chisel is a Python library for optimizing DNA sequences with respect to a set of constraints and optimization objectives. It comes with over 15 classes of sequence specifications which can be composed to, for instance, codon-optimize genes, meet the constraints of a commercial DNA provider, avoid homologies between sequences, tune GC content, or all of this at once!","addition_date":"2020-01-14T19:39:26Z","last_update_date":"2020-12-22T09:22:42Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library","Web application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:DNA_Chisel","edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Editing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3096"},{"term":"Nucleic acid design","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3095"}]}],"name":"DNA Chisel","owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1101/2019.12.16.877480"},{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btaa558","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2020 The Author(s) 2020. Published by Oxford University Press. All rights reserved.Motivation: Accounting for biological and practical requirements in DNA sequence design often results in challenging optimization problems. Current software solutions are problem-specific and hard to combine. Results: DNA Chisel is an easy-to-use, easy-to-extend sequence optimization framework allowing to freely define and combine optimization specifications via Python scripts or Genbank annotations.","authors":[{"name":"Rosser S."},{"name":"Zulkower V."}],"citationCount":3,"date":"2020-08-15T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"DNA Chisel, a versatile sequence optimizer"},"pmid":"32647895"}],"topic":[{"term":"DNA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0654"},{"term":"Gene expression","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0203"